### What happens when the size is exceeded?

The failure depends on which layer catches it first.

```java
package com.bank.error;

public class SizeExceeded {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Layer 1 -- Producer (max.request.size):");
        System.out.println("  Record > 1 MB -> RecordTooLargeException");
        System.out.println("  Fails LOCALLY, nothing sent to broker");
        System.out.println();
        System.out.println("Layer 2 -- Broker (message.max.bytes):");
        System.out.println("  Batch > broker limit -> rejected");
        System.out.println("  Producer sees error response");
        System.out.println();
        System.out.println("Layer 3 -- Consumer (max.partition.fetch.bytes):");
        System.out.println("  Record stored but fetch size too small");
        System.out.println("  Consumer STALLS on that partition");
    }
}
```

```text
Layer 1 -- Producer (max.request.size):
  Record > 1 MB -> RecordTooLargeException
  Fails LOCALLY, nothing sent to broker

Layer 2 -- Broker (message.max.bytes):
  Batch > broker limit -> rejected
  Producer sees error response

Layer 3 -- Consumer (max.partition.fetch.bytes):
  Record stored but fetch size too small
  Consumer STALLS on that partition
```

### How do you raise the limits?

All layers must be raised together, plus the replica fetcher.

```java
package com.bank.config;

public class RaiseLimits {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int targetSize = 5 * 1024 * 1024;  // 5 MB
        System.out.println("Target: " + targetSize + " bytes (5 MB)");
        System.out.println();
        System.out.println("Producer:");
        System.out.println("  max.request.size = " + targetSize);
        System.out.println();
        System.out.println("Broker/Topic:");
        System.out.println("  message.max.bytes = " + targetSize);
        System.out.println("  max.message.bytes = " + targetSize + " (per-topic)");
        System.out.println("  replica.fetch.max.bytes = " + targetSize);
        System.out.println();
        System.out.println("Consumer:");
        System.out.println("  max.partition.fetch.bytes = " + targetSize);
        System.out.println("  fetch.max.bytes = " + (50 * 1024 * 1024));
    }
}
```

```text
Target: 5242880 bytes (5 MB)

Producer:
  max.request.size = 5242880

Broker/Topic:
  message.max.bytes = 5242880
  max.message.bytes = 5242880 (per-topic)
  replica.fetch.max.bytes = 5242880

Consumer:
  max.partition.fetch.bytes = 5242880
  fetch.max.bytes = 52428800
```

### How does compression help?

```java
package com.bank.compression;

public class CompressionBenefit {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("JSON statement for Priya's account:");
        System.out.println("  Uncompressed : 3.2 MB (exceeds 1 MB limit)");
        System.out.println("  With zstd    : 0.6 MB (under limit!)");
        System.out.println();
        System.out.println("props.put(ProducerConfig.COMPRESSION_TYPE_CONFIG, \"zstd\")");
        System.out.println("No limit changes needed for this statement");
    }
}
```

